    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42437" root="يبس" body-key="Y">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايبست الأَرْضُ</span></b>  <i>The land had its plants</i> or
<i>herbage,</i> (A,) or <i>its leguminous plants,</i> (Yaakoob,
S, K,) <i>drying up,</i> or <i>dried up:</i> (Yaakoob, S, A,
K:) or <i>became abundant in its dry plants</i> or
<i>herbage.</i> (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايبست النَّاقَةُ</span> <i>The she-camel
became milkless.</i> (TA, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَجَّبَتْ</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايبس</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القَوْمُ</span> <i>The people journeyed in the land:</i> (K:)
or <i>in the dry land;</i> (TA;) like as you say
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَجْرَزُوا</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الأَرْضُ الجُرُزُ</span>. (S, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَيْبِسْ</span>:
see 1, last signification. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ايبسهُ</span>: see 2, in two
places.


